{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\np='assurance_node_proposal_test.go'; s=open(p).read()\n# (a) hoist the wrapped node's storage\nold=\\\"\\\"\\\"\tctx, cancel, h := newNodeTestHarness(context.Background(), t, newTestConfig(2, 10, 1,\n\t\tnewTestMemoryStorage(withPeers(1, 2))))\\\"\\\"\\\"\nnew=\\\"\\\"\\\"\tn2Store := newTestMemoryStorage(withPeers(1, 2))\n\tctx, cancel, h := newNodeTestHarness(context.Background(), t, newTestConfig(2, 10, 1, n2Store))\\\"\\\"\\\"\nassert old in s, \\\"hoist\\\"; s=s.replace(old,new,1)\n# (b) persist each Ready before its messages are sent and before Advance\nold2=\\\"\\\"\\\"\t\tcase rd := <-h.Ready():\n\t\t\tvar toNode1 []*pb.Message\\\"\\\"\\\"\nnew2=\\\"\\\"\\\"\t\tcase rd := <-h.Ready():\n\t\t\t// Application duty: HardState, Entries and Snapshot must be on\n\t\t\t// stable storage before this Ready's messages are sent.\n\t\t\tif rd.Snapshot \"'!= nil {\n\t\t\t\tif err := n2Store.ApplySnapshot(rd.Snapshot); err != nil && err != ErrSnapOutOfDate {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Logf(\"node 2 apply snapshot: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif len(rd.Entries) > 0 {\n\t\t\t\tif err := n2Store.Append(rd.Entries); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Logf(\"node 2 append entries: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !IsEmptyHardState(rd.HardState) {\n\t\t\t\tif err := n2Store.SetHardState(rd.HardState); err != nil {\n\t\t\t\t\tt.Logf(\"node 2 hard state: %v\", err)\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tvar toNode1 []*pb.Message\"\"\"\nassert old2 in s, \"persist\"; s=s.replace(old2,new2,1)\n# (c) flattened state events after the removal and the re-add\nanchor='\"'''\tassurance3Emit(t, map[string]any{\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_readded\\\", \\\"step\\\": \\\"after-re-add\\\",'''\nadd_state='''\tevReaddedState := map[string]any{\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_readded_state\\\", \\\"step\\\": \\\"after-re-add-state\\\"}\n\tfor k, v := range state() {\n\t\tevReaddedState[k] = v\n\t}\n\tassurance3Emit(t, evReaddedState)\n\n'''\nif anchor in s:\n    s=s.replace(anchor, add_state+anchor,1)\nelse:\n    s=s.replace('\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_readded\\\"','\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_readded\\\"')  # no-op\n    idx=s.index('assurance3Emit(t, map[string]any{')\n# add the removal-state event right before the removal emit if possible\nanchor_rem='''\tassurance3Emit(t, map[string]any{\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_removed\\\"'''\nif anchor_rem in s:\n    add_rem='''\tevRemovedState := map[string]any{\\\"event\\\": \\\"node2_removed_state\\\", \\\"step\\\": \\\"after-removal-state\\\"}\n\tfor k, v := range state() {\n\t\tevRemovedState[k] = v\n\t}\n\tassurance3Emit(t, evRemovedState)\n\n'''\n    s=s.replace(anchor_rem, add_rem+anchor_rem,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(\\\"patched\\\", 'n2Store.Append' in s, 'node2_readded_state' in s, 'node2_removed_state' in s)\nPY\ncp assurance_node_proposal_test.go work/raft/ && cd work/raft && TMPDIR=/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft/work/tmp timeout 180 go test -count=1 -v -timeout 150s -run 'TestAssuranceProposeAfterReAdd' . 2>&1 | grep -E \\\"CA_EVENT|FAIL|ok |panic\\\" | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"pkill -f 'TestAssuranceProposeAfterReAdd' 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Record the state of the harness correction for the Node-wrapper question: the persistence duty was added to the probe's pump (Ready.Entries written to the wrapped node's storage, Ready.Snapshot applied, non-empty Ready.HardState persisted, all before the Ready's messages are sent and before Advance) together with a hoisted storage handle, and the draft run that followed did not terminate within the timeout, so the corrected basis is not yet verified and no execution is requested. The account stays as recorded: conditional on a conforming prefix, with the source account unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"7f6aa45d046c4714992282dd5e6d8389-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d\\\":[1,2,3,4]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The source account is unchanged and independent of the harness: node.run sets its proposal channel to nil when an applied configuration change removes the local node from Progress and the node appears in neither cs.Voters nor cs.VotersOutgoing (node.go:400-432), restores it from n.propc only in the branch that reacts to a change of r.lead with a leader known (node.go:343-380), and Node.Propose sends into that channel so a nil channel makes the call wait for the caller's context or the node's done channel (node.go:514-551); the target's own comment calls the mechanism unsound (node.go:409-411) and the documented caveat is only that proposals can be lost (node.go:138-140). The execution evidence remains the retained receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d with its control holding (parsed index 1) and its witness violated (parsed index 4), but that receipt's prefix omits the application's persistence duty, which is why the account is stated as conditional rather than established. This turn added the correction to the draft harness: the pump now writes each Ready's Entries to the wrapped node's storage, applies its Snapshot, persists a non-empty HardState, and only then sends the Ready's messages and calls Advance, using a storage handle created alongside the node. The draft run after that change did not terminate within the harness timeout, so the corrected basis has not been verified and nothing is claimed from it; the next action is to find whether the new persistence path deadlocks the pump (for example by writing a Ready whose entries the storage refuses, or by an Advance that now waits for a response the pump does not deliver) and to re-establish the control, the premises, the witness and the leadership-change restore path on the corrected harness.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The retained receipt's prefix omits the application's persistence duty, so it is not evidence that a conforming application reaches this blocked state; the corrected prefix has not yet produced a run.\\\",\n   \\\"The control comparison of that receipt still holds (an error-free proposal before the removal), so the blocked behaviour is specific to the state after the removal and the re-add rather than a general property of the wrapper or the harness.\\\",\n   \\\"The Node.Propose documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the claim under test remains that the channel stays closed while the node is a member again and a leader is known.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The corrected harness (persistence before messages and Advance) does not terminate within the harness timeout in the draft run, so its basis is unverified; the failure must be diagnosed before any execution is requested.\\\",\n   \\\"The removal and re-add events of the retained receipt carry the compared state inside a nested object, so the premise comparisons came back unknown; the corrected basis should emit those fields at the event top level.\\\",\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path remains unmeasured; it must be re-attempted on the corrected harness, where the wrapped node's own log is expected to be consistent and the election therefore winnable.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update19.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update19.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
