{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Record the state of the harness correction for the Node-wrapper question: the probe's pump now writes each Ready's Entries to the wrapped node's storage, applies its Snapshot, persists a non-empty HardState, and only then sends the Ready's messages and calls Advance (with a storage handle created next to the node), because the retained receipt's prefix had omitted that application duty. The draft run after the change did not terminate within the harness timeout, so the corrected basis is unverified and no execution is requested; the account stays conditional and the source account unchanged.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"7f6aa45d046c4714992282dd5e6d8389-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d\\\":[1,2,3,4]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"conditional\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The source account is unchanged and independent of the harness: node.run sets its proposal channel to nil when an applied configuration change removes the local node from Progress and the node appears in neither cs.Voters nor cs.VotersOutgoing (node.go:400-432), restores it from n.propc only in the branch that reacts to a change of r.lead with a leader known (node.go:343-380), and Node.Propose sends into that channel, so a nil channel makes the call wait for the caller's context or the node's done channel (node.go:514-551); the target's own comment calls the mechanism unsound (node.go:409-411) and the documented caveat is only that proposals can be lost (node.go:138-140). The execution evidence is still receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d, whose control holds (parsed index 1) and whose witness is violated (parsed index 4), but that receipt's prefix omits the application's persistence duty, which is why the account is stated as conditional rather than established. This turn added the correction to the draft harness and the draft run that followed did not terminate within the harness timeout, so the corrected basis is unverified and nothing is claimed from it; the next action is to find whether the new persistence path deadlocks the pump (a Ready whose entries the storage refuses, or an Advance that now waits for something the pump does not deliver) and then to re-establish the control, the premises, the witness and the leadership-change restore path on the corrected harness.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The retained receipt's prefix omits the application's persistence duty, so it is not evidence that a conforming application reaches this blocked state, and the corrected prefix has not yet produced a run.\\\",\n   \\\"The control comparison of that receipt still holds (an error-free proposal before the removal), so the blocked behaviour is specific to the state after the removal and the re-add rather than a general property of the wrapper or the harness.\\\",\n   \\\"The Node.Propose documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the claim under test remains that the channel stays closed while the node is a member again and a leader is known.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The corrected harness does not terminate within the harness timeout in the draft run, so its basis is unverified and must be diagnosed before an execution is requested.\\\",\n   \\\"The removal and re-add events of the retained receipt carry the compared state inside a nested object, so those premise comparisons came back unknown; the corrected basis should emit those fields at the event top level.\\\",\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path remains unmeasured; it must be re-attempted on the corrected harness, where the wrapped node's own log is expected to be consistent and the election therefore winnable.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update19.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nprint('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update19.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
